  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 124 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nA ridge over Mexico will be the main driver in our weather \nthrough this week, amplifying and elongating its axis over Texas \nthrough Saturday, leading to warm, rain-free, and mostly clear to \npartly cloudy conditions. High temperatures will generally stay in\nthe 80s with low temperatures well into the 50s tonight, creeping\nback into the lower 60s by this weekend.\n\nShortwave disturbances from a mid-level low over the Four Corners \nregion moving northeast will bring our next low rain chances (20-\n30%) early next week, mainly over the Rio Grande Plains and Southern \nEdwards Plateau. We'll also see an increase in our cloud cover, \nreducing our high temperatures across South-Central Texas by a \ncouple degrees.",
